MVC Architecture of the Nutrition Assistant Application:
--------------------------------------------------------

The Nutrition Assistant backend application follows the **Model-View-Controller (MVC)** architectural pattern. MVC is a software design pattern that separates an application into three interconnected layers, making the application more modular, maintainable, scalable, and easier to develop.


Model Layer (Data Layer):
-------------------------

• The Model layer is responsible for handling all data-related operations.

• It defines the database structure using Mongoose schemas.

• The Model layer performs database operations such as:
  - Creating Data
  - Reading Data
  - Updating Data
  - Deleting Data (CRUD)

• Mongoose is used as the Object Data Modeling (ODM) library for interacting with the MongoDB database.

• Each model represents an entity in the application, such as:
  - User
  - Food
  - Diet Plan
  - Meal
  - Nutrition Record


Controller Layer:
-----------------

• The Controller layer acts as the bridge between the Routes (View Layer) and the Models (Data Layer).

• It receives incoming HTTP requests from the client.

• The controller performs:
  - Request Validation
  - Business Logic Processing
  - Data Transformation (if required)

• It communicates with the appropriate model to retrieve or update data.

• Finally, it sends an appropriate HTTP response back to the client.


View Layer (Routing Layer):
---------------------------

• In a REST API backend, the View layer is implemented through Express Routes.

• Routes define API endpoints for handling client requests.

• Supported HTTP methods include:
  - GET
  - POST
  - PUT
  - DELETE

• Each route maps a request to its corresponding controller function.

• The routing layer ensures that requests are directed to the correct business logic.


Advantages of Using MVC in This Project:
----------------------------------------

• Separation of Concerns
  - Each layer has a specific responsibility, making the code easier to understand, maintain, and extend.

• Scalability
  - New modules, routes, controllers, and models can be added without affecting existing functionality.

• Reusability
  - Business logic and database operations can be reused across different parts of the application.

• Testability
  - Models, controllers, and routes can be tested independently, improving software quality and reliability.

• Collaboration-Friendly
  - Multiple developers can work simultaneously on different layers of the application with minimal code conflicts.

• Maintainability
  - Code updates and bug fixes become easier because responsibilities are clearly separated.

• Better Project Organization
  - Files are organized into Models, Controllers, and Routes, making the project structure clean and easy to navigate.


Summary:
--------

The Nutrition Assistant Application follows the MVC architecture to ensure a well-structured, scalable, and maintainable backend. The Model manages database operations, the Controller processes application logic, and the View (Routing Layer) handles client requests. This architecture improves code organization, supports team collaboration, and simplifies future enhancements.
